Guard against a NULL pa_card_info::active_profile in libgvc's update_card().

PulseAudio leaves pa_card_info::active_profile NULL when a card has no usable
profile. pipewire-pulse surfaces this as

  mod.protocol-pulse: card 54 port N profiles inconsistent (0 < 3)

which happens on this machine every time a Thunderbolt dock's audio devices are
enumerated or torn down. update_card() then dereferences info->active_profile
unconditionally and gnome-shell segfaults:

  .gnome-shell-wr[3192]: segfault at 0 ip ... in libgvc.so
  #0  _pa_context_get_card_info_by_index_cb  (libgvc.so)   [update_card inlined]
  #1  context_get_card_info_callback         (libpulse.so.0)
  #2  run_action                             (libpulsecommon)

The faulting instruction confirms the field:

  49 8b 42 30   mov rax,[r10+0x30]   ; info->active_profile  (== NULL)
  48 8b 30      mov rsi,[rax]        ; active_profile->name  -> SIGSEGV

0x30 is the offset of active_profile in pa_card_info, and name is the first
member of pa_card_profile_info.

Both dereferences are guarded. The second skips the call rather than passing NULL
through, because gvc_mixer_card_set_profile() would then crash in g_str_equal().

Applies to gnome-shell's vendored subprojects/gvc; the same code is present in
libgnome-volume-control master.
--- a/subprojects/gvc/gvc-mixer-control.c
+++ b/subprojects/gvc/gvc-mixer-control.c
@@ -2608,7 +2608,8 @@
                 struct pa_card_profile_info pi = info->profiles[i];
                 gboolean is_default;
 
-                is_default = (g_strcmp0 (pi.name, info->active_profile->name) == 0);
+                is_default = info->active_profile != NULL &&
+                             (g_strcmp0 (pi.name, info->active_profile->name) == 0);
                 g_debug ("\tProfile '%s': %d sources %d sinks%s",
                          pi.name, pi.n_sources, pi.n_sinks,
                          is_default ? " (Current)" : "");
@@ -2646,7 +2647,12 @@
         gvc_mixer_card_set_profiles (card, profile_list);
         gvc_mixer_card_set_name (card, pa_proplist_gets (info->proplist, "device.description"));
         gvc_mixer_card_set_icon_name (card, pa_proplist_gets (info->proplist, "device.icon_name"));
-        gvc_mixer_card_set_profile (card, info->active_profile->name);
+        /* PulseAudio leaves active_profile NULL for a card with no usable profile
+         * (pipewire-pulse reports this as "profiles inconsistent"), e.g. while a
+         * USB/dock audio device is being torn down or enumerated. Passing NULL on
+         * would crash in gvc_mixer_card_set_profile()'s g_str_equal() anyway. */
+        if (info->active_profile != NULL)
+                gvc_mixer_card_set_profile (card, info->active_profile->name);
 
         if (is_new) {
                 g_hash_table_insert (control->priv->cards,
